.TH "CSDLC-WORKFLOW" "1" "September 11, 2026" "C-SDLC v3" "ADL Operator Manual"
.SH NAME
csdlc\-workflow \- prepare, execute, publish and reconcile one issue
.SH CANDIDATE ISSUE INTENT SEQUENCE
\&Semantic issue intent forms are the current operational contract. Direct issue\-writer \-\-request forms are retired and remain available only through \-\-help and \-\-describe for migration discovery. Observation and administrative request forms retain their documented contracts. See docs/csdlc\-v3/INTENT_COMMANDS.md for strict content and effect boundaries.
.nf
\&csdlc status ISSUE
\&csdlc prepare ISSUE \-\-plan PLAN.json
\&csdlc bind ISSUE
\&csdlc edit ISSUE \-\-changes CHANGES.json
\&csdlc validate ISSUE
\&csdlc proof ISSUE
\&csdlc review ISSUE \-\-evidence REVIEW.json
\&csdlc publish ISSUE
\&# Merge only after explicit exact\-target authorization and native admission.
\&csdlc finish ISSUE
\&csdlc clean ISSUE
\&csdlc clean ISSUE \-\-execute \-\-preview TOKEN
.fi
.PP
\&Supply issue\-specific six\-card values from the active templates, admitted validators and canonical publication content. Independent review is external evidence, never an automatically generated approval. Finish requires already merged/closed remote truth; cleanup is a separate token\-bound operation. Direct writer request syntax is retired; use positional intents or the declared intent request contract. Read\-only diagnostic requests remain supported.
.SH PRECONDITIONS
\&Use an existing tracked issue, accepted prerequisites and a reviewed issue\-specific plan. Check clean primary main and actual registrations; preserve another session's checkout. Commands below are templates using your own reviewed request files, not permission to mutate example IDs. Use the active installed binary by absolute path after changing checkouts.
.PP
\&Optional documentation helper: cargo run \-\-quiet \-\-manifest\-path csdlc\-v3/Cargo.toml \-\-example operator_manual \-\- ACTION PATH. Actions selector\-digest, review\-digest, file\-digest and registrations only read and print. It requires the pinned Rust toolchain/dependencies and is not installed as a lifecycle owner. It calls the current native public digest functions; it does not authenticate authored receipts.
.SH 1 PREPARE
.nf
\&git status \-\-short \-\-branch
\&git worktree list \-\-porcelain
\&csdlc prepare ISSUE \-\-plan plan.json
\&csdlc edit ISSUE \-\-changes design\-edit.json
\&csdlc validate ISSUE
\&csdlc doctor \-\-request current.json \-\-registry docs/templates/prompts/current.json \-\-registrations registrations.json
.fi
.PP
\&Store invocation files under the resolved primary Git metadata csdlc\-v3/local/invocations/ISSUE, not untracked primary artifacts. prepare.json uses LocalPreparationRequest from csdlc\-requests(1), the existing issue identity and proposed approved branch/worktree, registry version from current.json, full required commands and no initial expected digest.
.PP
\&Native issue creates six template\-based cards. Set design\-edit.json.card_updates to issue\-specific values from the active template field schemas using the relevant card\-editor skills. Preserve SIP/STP/SPP design truth, select proportional VPP lane, and leave review/output completion unclaimed. Before each following command refresh expected_lifecycle_digest from actual LOCAL_ROOT/issues/ISSUE/index.json.digest. Readiness dimensions must reflect observed prerequisites, path ownership and budget.
.PP
\&Generate registrations.json from actual Git topology using the optional registrations helper. Read every returned finding. A schema\-valid generic template is not an accepted design.
.PP
\&An issue with no native record uses the same prepare command and a complete six\-card plan. For a retained pre\-semantic native\-v3 record, prepare is an explicit compatibility operation: the owner fences the exact issue writer and accepts either a structurally complete unbound ready record or an already\-bound record whose common and linked bindings, registered branch, worktree, current head, generation, digest, cards and completion chain all agree. Pending, damaged, ambiguous or differently owned state is rejected without mutation. Every retained source byte remains in place, and an interrupted activation converges through an identical prepare replay. Before semantic preparation, status and edit may report intent_semantic_migration_required; after successful preparation, status separately reports card structure, dependency readiness and execution readiness. Existing\-issue GitHub mutation previews apply the same semantic admission as execution and therefore expose missing preparation instead of reporting ready.
.SH 2 BIND
.nf
\&csdlc bind ISSUE
\&cd /absolute/approved/issue\-worktree
\&csdlc doctor \-\-request current.json \-\-registry docs/templates/prompts/current.json \-\-registrations registrations.json
.fi
.PP
\&Verify the exact native bound branch, returned worktree, phase and six cards. Refresh current.json from the worktree .csdlc/issues/ISSUE/index.json and refresh registrations after bind. Use an absolute installed binary path or configured PATH. Create the issue\-bound session goal before implementation; keep root main inspection\-only.
.SH 3 IMPLEMENT AND REVIEW
\&Implement only planned paths, execute VPP's smallest meaningful proof, update SPP if the plan changes and SOR with actual results through native edit/validate. Commit the intended source and evidence so review binds an exact head. Obtain independent review at that exact revision; resolve actionable findings and renew proof/review after source changes.
.PP
\&Record one actual independent review judgment using csdlc.v3.review_judgment.v1: implementer, reviewer, reviewed_revision, verdict and evidence. The tool derives receipt and proof digests. PR metadata changes preserve current candidate validation and review; scope, validator and source changes still require appropriate fresh evidence.
.nf
\&csdlc review ISSUE \-\-evidence review\-evidence.json
.fi
.PP
\&The ordinary issue review command derives the native request and retains judgment plus receipt together. No manual dispatch wrapper or digest helper is needed. Historical native receipts remain readable.
.SH 4 CREATE AND VERIFY THE PR
.nf
\&csdlc review ISSUE \-\-evidence REVIEW.json
\&git push \-u origin YOUR_REVIEWED_BRANCH
\&csdlc publish ISSUE
\&csdlc pr\-state ISSUE
.fi
.PP
\&Push the exact reviewed branch before publication. Native publication verifies the authenticated remote branch head and does not push Git refs; a missing or changed remote head blocks dispatch.
.PP
\&Publication resolves the exact reviewed head and accepted base, title, body and draft metadata. Correct metadata with csdlc edit ISSUE \-\-changes publication.json before renewed proof and independent review. The changes use schema csdlc.v3.intent_changes.v1 and one publication object with base, title, body and draft. Closes #ISSUE must begin a line. Preparation rejects malformed metadata. Do not use retired github\-pr \-\-request writer syntax.
.PP
\&Metadata amendments preserve issue and binding identity and current candidate validation/review. Publication state is invalidated. Older proof records without candidate\-input identity need fresh proof after an input\-version change. After publication, base and draft cannot change through this editor. Verify actual base/head and closing linkage immediately after publication.
.PP
\&To transition from draft after required proof, use csdlc github\-pr ISSUE \-\-operation ready\-operation.json \-\-execute with action pull_request_ready. A published PR remains open/unmerged until explicitly authorized merge.
.SH 5 MERGE ONLY WITH AUTHORIZATION
\&Confirm required checks actually pass, unresolved review threads are resolved, current review is exact and the operator authorized this numeric PR merge. Use mutation pull_request_merge only through github\-pr with explicit base, method merge and current review receipt path/digest. Put the actual authorization reference in operator_approval; text alone is not approval.
.nf
\&csdlc github\-pr ISSUE \-\-operation merge\-operation.json \-\-execute
.fi
.PP
\&Retain authenticated reconciliation. Unsupported branch policy, incomplete observations or head/base/check drift stay blocked. All retries after merge intent are observation\-only; do not delete the guard or send a second raw merge.
.SH 6 FINISH
.nf
\&csdlc finish ISSUE
.fi
.PP
\&Use TerminalRouteRequest repository/issue/numeric PR/expected_head_sha/mode closing and credential_names. To persist terminal truth include terminal_state with actual reconciliation root and exact canonical state/receipt locations from csdlc(1). Linked: .csdlc/v3/issues/ISSUE/terminal.json and .csdlc/evidence/ISSUE/terminal\-receipt.json. Primary: resolved Git metadata csdlc\-v3/local/v3/issues/ISSUE/terminal.json and csdlc\-v3/local/evidence/ISSUE/terminal\-receipt.json.
.PP
\&Finish independently observes merged PR, correct expected head and closed linked issue; no second GitHub mutation or closeout PR is needed. Retain returned terminal state/receipt and distinguish terminal observation from persistence when terminal_state is omitted.
.SH 7 CLEAN
.nf
\&csdlc clean ISSUE
\&csdlc clean ISSUE \-\-execute \-\-preview TOKEN
.fi
.PP
\&Before cleaning from primary, repeat the authenticated finish invocation from primary with terminal_state.repository_root set to that primary checkout and primary canonical Git\-metadata state/receipt paths. The linked finish receipt in step 6 is not a primary cleanup receipt: do not copy it or point primary cleanup at the linked .csdlc file. Retain the newly authenticated primary receipt and its byte digest.
.PP
\&Run clean from the primary, not the target you will remove. Supply the actual approved parent, primary repository root, exact registered candidate, expected head and that primary durable terminal receipt path/digest. First remove false; only a Removable result supplies the preview receipt for a second request with remove true and matching preview_receipt_digest.
.PP
\&Preserve dirty, live or unregistered work. The cleanup gate checks a live\-worktree marker and Git state; it is not a general host process scanner. Remove only the exact target and verify the returned Removed result. Do not broaden cleanup to other issue worktrees.
.SH RECOVERY
\&Local compare\-and\-swap drift: inspect actual current state and regenerate only the intended semantic edit with fresh digest. Interrupted transaction: retain original request and state, use the identical native mutator request, and route unresolved failures to bounded tooling repair. No handwritten index/journal recovery.
.PP
\&Remote uncertain response: same exact request, same target and retained intent; native reconciliation observes the remote effect. An uncertain result is not a successful publication, merge or finish. Read csdlc\-github\-pr(1) for merge\-specific one\-shot dispatch semantics.
.PP
\&This manual's schema fixtures prove request shape and selected guard/plan behavior. They do not claim an end\-to\-end live GitHub deployment or authorize example targets.
